{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "My recent trip to Japan was a sensory overload in the best possible way. From the moment I arrived in Tokyo, I was struck by the vibrant energy of the city. The neon lights of Shinjuku's skyscrapers gave way to the tranquil gardens of the Meiji Shrine, a serene oasis in the midst of the bustling metropolis.\n\nAs I traveled through the country, I was amazed by the contrasts that Japan embodies. Ancient temples and shrines stood alongside cutting-edge technology and innovative design. In Kyoto, I marveled at the stunning beauty of the Fushimi Inari shrine, with its thousands of vermilion torii gates forming a tunnel up the mountain.\n\nBut it was the people of Japan who truly made my trip unforgettable. Everywhere I went, I was met with kindness and courtesy. From the friendly shopkeepers in the markets to the courteous staff at the ryokans (traditional inns), the Japanese culture of respect and hospitality shone through.\n\nOne of the highlights of my trip was a traditional tea ceremony in a serene garden. The delicate rituals and precise movements of the ceremony were a beautiful reflection of the country's attention to detail and appreciation for the simple things in life.\n\nAs I left Japan, I felt grateful for the experience and already planning my next trip back. Japan is a country that will continue to captivate and inspire me, and I look forward to returning soon.", "logprobs": [{"token": "My", "logprob": -0.46528711915016174}, {"token": " recent", "logprob": -0.00416210200637579}, {"token": " trip", "logprob": -7.152531907195225e-06}, {"token": " to", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -6.556489552167477e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.20399625599384308}, {"token": " sensory", "logprob": -1.5810136795043945}, {"token": " overload", "logprob": -0.035803280770778